# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Root .gitignore for the Contextle monorepo.
# Sub-projects (frontend/) may keep their own .gitignore as well.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json

# --- Secrets / environment ---
# Never commit real env files. Example files (.env.example) ARE committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- Node / Next.js (frontend) ---
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
.vercel/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
coverage/
.env.local

# --- Python (backend + ml) ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- uv ---
# uv.lock IS committed (reproducible installs); caches are not.
.uv/

# --- ML artifacts (never commit models / datasets / checkpoints) ---
# See AGENTS.md: heavy model files, datasets and checkpoints stay out of Git.
ml/data/*
!ml/data/.gitkeep
!ml/data/README.md
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.npy
*.npz
.cache/
models/
checkpoints/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Deployment smoke artifact (narrow exception to `*.npy` above) ---
# `backend/artifacts/` holds the small rank-artifact root that ships *inside*
# the backend image, because Docker `COPY` cannot reach outside the build
# context (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md). It is deployment data, not ML output: ~4 MiB
# over 20 arrays, versioned so the image is reproducible from the commit alone.
#
# Scoped to this directory on purpose. The rule above still keeps every array
# under `ml/` out of Git, and this exception is NOT a policy that artifact roots
# belong in the repository — the final production root is far larger and needs
# a real distribution channel (see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md).
!backend/artifacts/**/*.npy

# --- Docker ---
# (compose files and Dockerfiles are committed; local overrides are not)
docker-compose.override.yml

# --- Agent tooling (oh-my-claudecode) ---
# Runtime state: session logs, plans, handoffs, notepad. Ignored in any
# sub-project. Project-scoped skills under .omc/skills/ stay committable, so
# the contents are ignored rather than the directory itself.
**/.omc/*
!**/.omc/skills/
